Features.DataBinding.Index
  Data[]
    Data:Users https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users
  SimpleStack
    Header 2|Data Binding
    Text Databinding allows both one way and two way databinding with simple expressions.
    Text Markdown also supports any data binding expression, however the binding becomes read only.

    Header 2|Static Bindings (One Way)
    Text Static bindings are update once during initialization and not updated again.
    Text Static bindings are used to load resources and other items.

    Header 3|HTTP
    PreText [off]=HTTP(https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users)
    EditMulti =HTTP(https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users)
      Width: 300
      Height: 100

    Header 3|'' - Literal
    Text String literal. Useful only in corner cases.
    PreText [off]=''(Hello World)
    Text =''(Hello World)

    Header 3|URL
    Text Allows retrieval of a parameter in the URL of the request.

    Header 3|Code Call
    Text Allows a binding to call code to provide a value, or even modify data.
    Text 6 * 4: 

    Header 2|Dynamic Bindings (Two way)
    # Data and field in code

    Header 3|This - Code Property Binding
    Text These values are properties declared in the code file.
    PreText
      Text:
        MagicNo: [=this.MagicNo]
        Message: [=this.Message] [=this.MagicNo]
    Text If you change the values in code, the bindings update automatically. Push this button to see.
    Button:ThisButton Change

    Header 3|Prop
    Text Static if page only

    Header 3|Page
    Text Page allows access to the page versus code (this). The page contains its own list of controls.
    Text This is useful when there is no code behind to access Dataset EOF/BOF for example. See Advanced Data Binding Example.

    Header 2|JSON Data
    Text All of these samples are using this dataset.
    PreText Data:Users https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users
    Text This dataset is loaded by URL, but literal JSON can be embedded also.

    Header 3|Data (Default)
    Text The data tag is the default, so it can be specified as in the first exmaple:
    PreText [off]=data.Users.name 
    Text or omitted as in the other examples:
    PreText [off]=.Users.username / =.Users.email
    Text These are two way databindings. Changes are applied back to the dataset for easy REST or other CRUD.
    Text By default the cursor is on the first row, so these return data from the first row.
    Edit =data.Users.name
    Edit =.Users.username
    Edit =.Users.email
    Text Data tags also support locators allowing access to other rows without moving the cursor.
    Text Please see a demo wtih more Data bindings for examples.

    Header 3|*
    Text * is used with controls that iterate over rows in a dataset, such as repeaters. * signfies the current row.
    Text For more information, see a demo wtih a repeater.

    Header 3|ROWS
    Text ROWS is used to convert a single field into a string array, for use with look ups etc.
    Text For more information, see a demo wtih ROWS.
